---
alwaysApply: true
rules:
  - |
    ## Docs generation rule (read before editing)
    - Do NOT edit generated docs: `docs/**` and `<action>/README.md` (overwritten on release).
    - Only add hand-written action docs in `<action>/DOCS.md` (keep concise; do not duplicate generated sections).
    - Auto-generated sections (do NOT add these to `DOCS.md`): title/description, quick usage snippet, inputs table, outputs table, technical (`runs.*`) info, referenced actions, files list, other versions links.
    - Avoid H1 (`# ...`) in `DOCS.md` (generator strips H1 lines).
    - Do NOT edit the generated section of root `README.md` between `<!-- LATEST_TAGS_START -->` / `<!-- LATEST_TAGS_END -->`.

    ## How it’s generated (source of truth)
    - Trigger: `.github/workflows/release-action.yml`
    - Generator: `.github/workflows/scripts/generate_action_docs.py <action> <version>`
    - Sources: `action.yml` (+ optional `DOCS.md`)
    - Writes: `docs/<action>/<version>.md` + `<action>/README.md`
    - Also updates root `README.md` between `<!-- LATEST_TAGS_START -->` / `<!-- LATEST_TAGS_END -->`

    ## If docs must change
    - Change `action.yml` or `<action>/DOCS.md`; otherwise change the generator script (ask first for format/structure changes).

---
